  (text
    "Function: Connect four PCIe lanes to the PC using GTY225.\nOnly physical lanes0-3 are wired; lanes4-7 are NC.\n\nSource / changes: Opal Kelly BRK8310-A01 sheet2 (PCIe),\nhttps://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/442/download?category_id=3 .\nV7 removes C21-C26/C29/C30 and all upper-lane signal links.\nRetains BRK x8 mechanical edge and its x8 presence: R29 fitted,\nR27/R28 DNP. This is an electrical x4 link, not a new x4 outline.\nConfigure the PCIe IP for x4, GTY225 lanes3,2,1,0 = PCIe0,1,2,3.\nVivado placement/refclock and DMA/host operation remain open.\nAMD PG213, Artix UltraScale+ available GT quads:\nhttps://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/pg213-pcie4-ultrascale-plus/Artix-UltraScale-Devices-Available-GT-Quads"
    (at 1755.6 282.4 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "2d5163e2-18d9-5d65-b25b-04e3fb4666ca"))
  (rectangle
    (start 20.32 1158.24)
    (end 688.34 1493.52)
    (stroke (width 0.508) (type default))
    (fill (type none))
    (uuid "ba1db954-b881-5119-9da5-6b819d15fc52"))
