  (text
    "Function: J500 is the USB2 device input. CC1/CC2\nuse 5.1k pulldowns; shield uses 100nF and a\n220ohm@100MHz ferrite to GND. USB5V feeds\nthe FTDI core through the source filter.\n\nSource / changes: Codex extraction from the\nBRK8305 A03-derived Carrier_V1 J4 USB-C\nadaptation. Original BRK J500/R500/R501/\nFB503/C522; JTAG sheet8/PDFp4,25Oct2023:\nhttps://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/583/\ndownload?category_id=3\nGCT USB4110-GF-A revB4,22May2024,sheets1-2:\nhttps://gct.co/files/drawings/usb4110.pdf\nUSB4110 SMT shell pin mapping retained;\nsource optional LED/probes omitted. D500 adds data/VBUS ESD protection in the\nadjacent circuit. USB qualification pending."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 2023.84 256.0 0)
    (effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "33ffcd43-a8c9-45a3-bc3a-bff7673469f3"))
  (rectangle
    (start 2021.84 254.0)
    (end 2133.84 356.0)
    (stroke (width 0.254) (type default))
    (fill (type none))
    (uuid "65ab2d41-d23e-4fec-bcfe-b841c7cf3d04"))
  (text
    "Function: U501 is a USB2-to-JTAG MPSSE host. HOST_TCK/TDI/TMS\nare3.3V outputs; HOST_TDO is an input. U505 holds cable configuration;\nY500 is12MHz. FTDI3V3 is an internal regulator rail.\n\nSource / changes: BRK8305 A03,25Oct2023,JTAG sheet8/PDFp4:\nhttps://pins.opalkelly.com/downloads/583/download?category_id=3\nNative36-part wired core extracted from Carrier_V1; same core values,\nnew refs/rail names. AXC target shifters excluded. USBLC6 array and\nseparate selector LDO added in adjacent blocks. R508=10k adds a high\nADBUS4/VCCO_JTAG_ON input instead of source NC. Trenz primary\nimplementation notes14Jan2026 identify high/floating ADBUS4 and\noptional ADBUS6 PROG_B; Vivado2023.2/2024.2 tests passed:\nhttps://wiki.trenz-electronic.de/display/PD/AMD+FTDI+JTAG+Programmer\nADBUS5/6/7 remain unused; target programming uses JTAG.\nR509=10k holds HOST_TDO high when all target banks are isolated;\nCodex addition to the inherited core.\nFTDI DS_FT232H v2.2,6Sep2024,sections3.3,4.1,6:\nhttps://ftdichip.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/09/DS_FT232H.pdf\nStandard93LC56B-E/MS requires one-time AMD program_ftdi\nprovisioning per UG9082026.1,Programming FTDI Devices:\nhttps://docs.amd.com/r/en-US/ug908-vivado-programming-debugging/\nProgramming-FTDI-Devices-for-Vivado-Hardware-Manager-Support\nDo not invent or copy CFG001 image. First-board provisioning,\nVivado discovery and electrical operation require testing."
    (exclude_from_sim no)
    (at 2307.05 106.14 0)
    (effects (font (size 1 1)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "684be6b2-8b21-4f77-94e5-4ee5f9db2e2c"))
