  (text
    "Function: Two-position mode switch. ONBOARD powers the target-selector common and selects the USB XEM branch. EXTERNAL disables all eight onboard target branches and selects J3 for XEM recovery. No FPGA firmware is required.\n\nSource / changes: Codex master-control wiring; C&K/Littelfuse JS series datasheet rev. VL 01/14/26, JS202011JCQN vertical SMT drawing and DPDT circuit; https://www.littelfuse.com/assetdocs/littelfuse-c-k-slide-js-series-\ndatasheet?assetguid=aba42b08-0d2c-423b-813d-a2faa5a3bb14 . Local footprint preserves KiCad JS202011JCQN geometry but renumbers second-row pads 4/5/6 to manufacturer terminals 5/6/7. Separate switch poles keep USB3.3V and XEM1.8V control domains independent. Use J3\nwith a 1.8V-referenced external cable."
    (at 2200.1 627.84 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "c9eea40b-c88c-52ee-b05e-5e0528629abb"))
  (rectangle
