  (text
    "Function: Reference eight GT receivers from the actual module125MHz oscillator through dedicated adjacent-quad clock routes. PCIe uses the separate host100MHz reference.\n\nSource / changes: Existing XEM8310 on-module hardware: Opal Kelly BoardStore board.xml oscillator125 and part0_pins.xml V7/V6. https://github.com/opalkelly-opensource/XilinxBoardStore/tree/master/boards/OpalKelly/XEM8310-AU25P/1.0 . Codex V7 internal clock plan follows AMD UG578 v1.4 pp24-25 dedicated north/south reference paths: https://docs.amd.com/v/u/en-US/ug578-ultrascale-gty-transceivers . This diagram is an FPGA implementation plan, not new carrier copper.125MHz reaches one neighboring quad in each direction; run Vivado GT\nWizard/PCIe x4 placement before freezing implementation. External224/226REFCLK0 pins remain NC as fallback interfaces."
    (at 1325.07 1203.15 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid "d1fb241b-f267-5c48-89d6-532bce040694"))
  (text
